# The unit and list patterns of CLDR release 49 that `i18n/dates` writes a
# duration with, "3 hours, 5 minutes": for every locale CLDR holds, the
# patterns of ten units of time in three widths and six plural
# categories, the patterns that join a list of units in three widths, and
# the sizes of the digit groups of its decimal pattern.
#
# Every text is held once, in `TEXTS`. A row names each of its texts by
# three characters of base 64, the ten digits, the capital and the small
# letters, `+` and `/`, as `date_data.number_at` reads them.
#
# Generated, never edited by hand: the Heroes program
# `rebel/generators/i18n_units/` read CLDR 49's JSON,
# `cldr-49.0.0-json-full.zip` of
# https://github.com/unicode-org/cldr-json/releases/download/49.0.0/
# (SHA-256
# 3b1f5d684d29c541d3acf91fe834b3fe36ae0f34775e3ee50e93558bf14ca174,
# fetched 2026-11-21), its files `cldr-units-full/main/*/units.json`,
# `cldr-misc-full/main/*/listPatterns.json`,
# `cldr-numbers-full/main/*/numbers.json` and
# `cldr-core/availableLocales.json`, and wrote this module whole; its
# `check` command says whether this module is still what it writes.

# Every text a row names, once, in the order of their bytes; text 0 is the
# empty one, the pattern of a plural category a language does not use.
constant TEXTS: [str]
